[size=4][b][u]Overview[/u][/b][/size]
Creations Forge browses, compares, and edits FormLists in Bethesda plugins through a cross-platform desktop application. The source tree also includes a local MCP server for compatible clients.

Open explicit source plugins and their load order, then create or edit a separate output plugin. Source and load-order plugins remain inputs; Creations Forge stages authoring changes in the selected output workspace and applies save guards before publishing files.

[quote]
IMPORTANT: The FormList workflow replaces the earlier SQLite import workflow. Existing import databases are not converted into editable plugins, and no database reset or reimport is required. Removing the old backend does not delete existing database files.
[/quote]

[quote]
NOTE: Plugin FormList authoring is implemented for Fallout 4, Skyrim Special Edition, and Starfield. Packaged launches, installed-game coverage, Mod Organizer 2 and other virtual-file-system workflows, and game-runtime acceptance are not yet fully validated.
[/quote]

Please report bugs here: [url=https://github.com/monster-cookie/CreationsForge/issues]https://github.com/monster-cookie/CreationsForge/issues[/url]

[size=4][b][u]Features[/u][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Opens explicit source plugins and load order directly without importing records into an application database.[/*]
[*]Browses and compares FormLists across the active plugin context.[/*]
[*]Creates new FormLists, overrides source FormLists into an output plugin, and edits FormLists already staged in that output.[/*]
[*]Provides typed edit actions and reference lookup for linked records.[/*]
[*]Separates unapplied editor input, staged workspace changes, and saved output files.[/*]
[*]Reviews changes and warnings before saving or discarding staged work.[/*]
[*]Detects changed source or output files and blocks stale saves.[/*]
[*]Provides save-outcome inspection and recovery actions for interrupted or uncertain publication.[/*]
[*]Includes a local MCP server over standard input and standard output.[/*]
[*]Supports light and dark desktop themes.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b][u]Supported Games and Record Types[/u][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Fallout 4: FormList (FLST) authoring.[/*]
[*]Skyrim Special Edition: FormList (FLST) authoring.[/*]
[*]Starfield: FormList (FLST) authoring.[/*]
[/list]

Other record families may appear in reference lookup, but they are not supported authoring targets. This workflow does not provide general plugin editing, automatic conflict resolution, or asset preview.

[size=4][b][u]Desktop Usage[/u][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Launch Creations Forge and choose Open Workspace.[/*]
[*]Select Fallout 4, Skyrim Special Edition, or Starfield.[/*]
[*]Select a source plugin, game data directory, and explicit load order with required masters first and the source included.[/*]
[*]Choose whether to create a new output plugin or open an existing output plugin. Keep the output separate from the admitted source files.[/*]
[*]Select a FormList to compare, create a new FormList, override the selected source FormList, or edit a FormList already in staged output.[/*]
[*]Apply typed edit actions to staged output, then review changes and warnings.[/*]
[*]Choose Save Changes and confirm publication. Read any conflict, uncertain-outcome, or recovery message before continuing.[/*]
[/list]

Desktop and MCP workspaces are independent and do not synchronize live. If another workspace or application changes a source or output file, resolve the reported conflict instead of assuming those changes were adopted.

[size=4][b][u]MCP Usage[/u][/b][/size]
Configure a standard-input/standard-output MCP client to launch the console executable with the single argument [code]mcp[/code]. The client opens explicit workspaces and performs bounded FormList operations through the advertised tools. The removed game-import and database-reset arguments are not supported.

[size=4][b][u]Application Data and Logging[/u][/b][/size]

[size=3][b]Linux and macOS[/b][/size]
Application configuration and logs use ~/.CreationsForge. The macOS configuration path does not imply a validated macOS package.

[size=3][b]Windows[/b][/size]
Application configuration and logs use C:\ProgramData\CreationsForge.

[size=4][b][u]Installation[/u][/b][/size]
Use a desktop or console build that contains the plugin authoring replacement. Earlier releases may still contain the retired import workflow. Windows and Linux packaging exists in the source repository, but packaged plugin-workflow launches remain unverified.

Do not install the application into a game's Data folder. Keep source plugins, required masters, localized-string directories when needed, and the separate output location available while a workspace is open.

[size=4][b][u]Current Limitations[/u][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Plugin authoring is limited to FormLists for Fallout 4, Skyrim Special Edition, and Starfield.[/*]
[*]Saving edits to an existing localized output that uses separate string files is rejected to protect unedited localized data.[/*]
[*]An installed Starfield source has encountered an unresolved parser failure while reading navmesh data.[/*]
[*]Installed Fallout 4 and Skyrim Special Edition validation inputs have not yet been supplied.[/*]
[*]Plugin Mod Organizer 2 and other virtual-file-system workflows remain unverified.[/*]
[*]Packaged launches, live desktop/MCP conflict checks, and game-runtime acceptance remain unverified.[/*]
[/list]

